      "bc.fromTrackPage.one": "From the track page:",
      "bc.fromTrackPage.other": "From the track pages:",
      "bc.trackPageTitle": "Opens the track page on Bandcamp",
      "about.from": "From the “about” text",
      "liner.poolName": "Liner notes – {name}",
      "log.linerFound": "Liner notes found below the “about” text, signed “{name}” (the name only suggested)",
      "dgStatus.off": "click: skip this credit (its row goes to “Skip”)",
      "dgStatus.on": "click: take this credit again",
      "dgStatus.isOff": "switched off here",
      "bc.offNote": "Switched off on {site} (a click on its mark): “Skip”. Another click there switches it on again, so does choosing a level here.",
      "ms.3.17.0": "Bandcamp view in the companion (1.8.0): a Bandcamp tab follows the dashboard like a Discogs tab – status marks before each part of a credits line (album and track pages), a click on a mark shows its row, a row jumps to its line (from the “about” text: to its sentence), track highlight, status on the MusicBrainz release page; “open in background” and “Load the release there” for Bandcamp too. Rows from track pages link to them.",
      "ms.3.18.0": "Works matrix: “Skip works matrix” (kept for the release) – nothing of it is staged (no works, no links to works, no work relationships), its rows go to “Skip” and the work lookups rest; “Take works matrix again” brings it all back. The matrix folds and unfolds at its head. From 100 tracks without a work (setting) the works section asks before the work lookups, with about how long they take. “Add entry manually” is one line above the date pool, always in view.",
      "ms.3.21.0": "Text recognition, part 1: several sentences in one line are read one by one (“Graphic design: X. Text: Y. Produced by Z.”); “℗ & ©”, “P + ©” and “(P) & (C)” give both, without codes like “DDD” or catalogue numbers; web addresses are never part of a name – a profile (Instagram, SoundCloud …) after a name is looked up in MusicBrainz as a suggestion and filled in by “Create artist”, Linktree and other addresses are left out; “Logo by” is design with the credit “logo”; a title in quotation marks with its year before “by” and “courtesy of …” are no part of a credit; “Text: X” asks: liner notes or lyrics; thanks and endorsements are listed as left out on purpose.",
      "ms.3.22.0": "Text recognition, part 2: instruments and voices in German, Spanish and French (“Schlagzeug”, “batería”, “contrebasse”) become MusicBrainz's own names without a role credit, words with several meanings (“bajo”, “Alto”) are asked; tracks named by their titles in quotation marks (“Piano in ‘A’ and ‘B’ is a contribution by X”) are found on the release; “Recorded by X in Xixon, Asturies, Spain” gives X and the area where it was recorded (recorded, mixed or mastered in – found by its other names too, only suggested); credits for a medium the release does not have (“Vinyl LP mastering”) are left out, and each line left out on purpose says why; “Translated by” on Bandcamp suggests liner notes; artist pages of streaming services and profiles after labels and studios are filled in by “Create …”, the links at the entries are shown by a setting; large releases: every medium in the choice, the chosen ones loaded at once with MusicBrainz's own controls",
      "ms.3.27.0": "A clearer dashboard: the entries compact – one line per role (role → type and instrument, level, tracks, date), a click opens the row to change it; dates and track groups can still be dropped onto the line, what is open is in colour (red missing, yellow a question or suggestion), skipped rows are grey with ✕; “Compact | Full” is remembered. The head in one line with symbols of its own, “Source ▾” for everything about the source, “+ Supplement” only on request; the settings as tabs (also “Texts” and “ⓘ Connections” – every site, tool and script the script works with), “Reset all settings” in them; after the installation the language is asked once",
      "ms.3.29.0": "Text recognition, part 3: credits in prose (\"… by K.M. (sounds, words) & E. (voice)\", \"Cover artwork channeled by …\", \"Logo carved by the guided hand of …\"), every place of joined verbs (\"Mixed and mastered at …\") and lists of kinds (\"Tenor, alto, soprano saxophones\"); a date goes to every group of joined words and takes its group only from its own sentence, years of a release are left out, \"19 & 20. 01. 2009\" and \"1973 October 19\" are read; \"C1 to D\" with a side of one track, \"in live concert\" only for the tracks named. Since 3.27.0 also: Bandcamp track pages as releases; Norwegian, Swedish and Danish roles, \"Logo Og Kunst\" as design \"logo\" and artwork \"art\", \"cover design\", \"wood flutes\" as flute; no \"credited as\" when only the case differs, the spelling of a text when it differs; the companion underlines the dates and track groups used in the Discogs notes and on Bandcamp.",
      "ms.3.31.0": "Text recognition, part 4: publishers below a heading (\"[Publishers & Rights Societies] • FlizmoMusic-BMI : tracks 2, 4, 5\") on their tracks, their rights society (BMI, ASCAP, GEMA … – a list of the societies) on the release level, a publisher with the name of a person as a part of that person's column in the works matrix, names written together searched apart too (\"Flizmo Music\", \"Four Word Sea Music\"); the members of a band (\"Vision Fortune are A, B and C\") as performers, \"sounds\" asks performer or effects; from the Discogs notes dates per disc (\"May 26, 2016 (Disc 2)\"), places and the label of \"© & ℗ TUM Records Oy 2021\" (TUM Records offered too). Since 3.29.0 also: the mapping rules in the dashboard or as a window (also from a rule id at a row), colours for the levels, the level of a compact line switched by a click, ⚙ Settings → Appearance, an entry or a group compact at once, each pool folds on its own, scroll bars above and below the works matrix, the settings without an import (\"Source pages\"), the tracks of a track group typed in.",
      "ms.3.32.0": "Quick switches at the top of “Mapping rules”: a rights society after a writer’s name (“Composed by X (BMI)”) as the release’s rights society, Performance on several days as their common month or year (now the default), “live” for live releases, no “credited as” when only the case differs, festivals left out, dates in the titles of the tracks, “Performer” on tracks for the instruments (the last two off until switched on). Since 3.31.0 also: a person as publisher is a role of that person (artist–work “publishing”), a publisher’s row on the works or on the release, tracks from the notes set (ⓘ says where from), poems and poetry (lyricist, spoken vocals, asked when alone), the kind of engineer said twice (“Engineer [Recording Engineer]”), places from the notes looked up by name and area (“Loft Köln”), days with commas only (“November 7, 8, 2016”); Companion 1.9.1: the status marks and the cover box stay while MusicBrainz is in the background.",
      "ms.3.33.0": "The mapping file: the data of the mapping rules – role rules, company roles, questions, tables and word lists, the quick switches – is a file of its own, mb-vibecode-credits-importer-mapping.json, which the userscript manager loads with the script (and the script fetches from GitHub itself if not); rules can be kept on GitHub without touching the code. Also: places with a date after them, typos in role words, the credits of Bandcamp's “about” text, poems that follow their level, single days instead of a month, the quick switches as buttons, comments of live recordings.",
